4. RECEIVING JSON FROM THE CLIENT (POST): READING THE BODY IN CHUNKS
--------------------------------------------------------------------
The body arrives in pieces: append every chunk on 'data', use the result only on 'end'.

[ T6/server.js, lines 40-50 ]  read chunks until the end, then call the callback with the full body
```
 // Helper function to read a request body
 function readRequestBody(req, callback) {
    let body = ""
    req.on('data', (chunk) => {
        body += chunk.toString();
    })
    // Once the entire body is ready, process the request
    req.on('end', () => {
        callback(body);
    });
}
```

[ T6/server.js, lines 93-123 ]  parse the body, handle each POST route, answer with HTML or JSON
```
    //Handle the POST request
    if (request.method === "POST") {
