  - e.preventDefault() stops the browser's normal form submit.
  - Object.fromEntries(new FormData(this)) turns the form fields into {name: value, ...}.
  - fetch only rejects on a NETWORK failure (TypeError). A 404/500 still resolves, so check response.ok / response.status.
  - Server replies JSON -> response.json().  Server replies HTML -> response.text().


6. COMMON STATUS CODES
----------------------
  200 OK                     success (GET page/JSON, POST handled)
  201 Created                success, a new resource was created (often POST)
  204 No Content             success, nothing to send back
  301 / 302 Redirect         Location header says where to go
  400 Bad Request            client sent bad data (e.g. invalid JSON)
  401 / 403                  not logged in / not allowed
  404 Not Found              file or route doesn't exist
  500 Internal Server Error  server-side failure (fs error, template error, exception)

Used in your server (see the T6/server.js lines 21-39 block above): 200, 404 and 500.
The status is set with response.writeHead(status, headers) once, before response.end().


