4. CONVERSION CHECKLIST
-----------------------
  1. Replace the hard-coded title/stylesheet with variables; move repeated header/footer into partials.
  2. Anything client JS built with createElement (select options, table rows, menu lists)
     becomes a loop in the template using data passed from the server.
  3. If the browser script still needs the data, emit it with <%- JSON.stringify(x) %> / !{JSON.stringify(x)}.
  4. In server.js, pages go through renderPage(path, response, {data}); css/js/images stay on serveStaticFile.


5. ISSUES I FOUND IN YOUR OWN FILES (code above is shown unchanged, so these bugs are visible in it)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  - T6/server.js and T7/server.js: a POST to an unknown path never calls response.end(), so the request hangs.
    Also JSON.parse(body) throws on invalid JSON and would crash the server.
  - T7/views/reservations.pug line 18: option(value="=loc.name1 – =loc.name2") is a literal string
    ("=" is not evaluated inside quotes). It should be a JS expression, e.g. value=loc.name1 + " – " + loc.name2.
  - T7/views/reservations.ejs line 13: "// Populate the Select box..." is plain HTML text, not a comment
    (use <%# ... %> or <!-- ... -->).
  - T7/views/locations.ejs line 8: the inner loop has no `&& i<locations.length` (the pug version, line 10, does),
    so a location count that isn't a multiple of 3 gives an undefined `loc` and an error.
  - T7/views/menu.ejs line 1: the title says "Locations" instead of "Menu".
